<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmadou Ahidjo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924–1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmadou Ahidjo was a Cameroonian politician from the Muslim north who became prime minister of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a> in 1958 and led it to independence in 1960. As first president of Cameroon he united it with the former British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-cameroons">Southern Cameroons</a> in 1961, created a one-party state and ruled until he resigned in 1982 in favour of Paul Biya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmadou-ahidjo.jpg" alt="Ahmadou Ahidjo" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Series: Reagan White House Photographs, 1/20/1981 - 1/20/1989 Collection: White House Photographic Collection, 1/20/1... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmadou_Ahidjo_visits_the_White_House_on_July_26,_1982.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
